{
  "id": "hoysala",
  "title": "The Hoysalas",
  "description": "An illustrated map of the Hoysalas of Karnataka, who rose from hill chiefs to rule the southern Deccan, built the star-shaped temples of Belur, Halebidu and Somanathapura, and fell to Delhi’s armies and the Madurai Sultanate by 1343.",
